ame></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUKAWA, TETSUYA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATAKE, HIDESHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI, MASATO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TERANO, MINORU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUKAWA TETSUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATAKE HIDESHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI MASATO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TERANO MINORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUKAWA, TETSUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATAKE, HIDESHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI, MASATO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TERANO, MINORU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A propylene/ethylene block copolymer which has a poly(ethylene-co-propylene) segment content of 5 to 100 wt.%, excluding 100 wt.%, and a total ethylene content of 2 to 95 wt.%. (a) It comprises polypropylene segments and chemically bonded thereto poly(ethylene-co-propylene) segments, and (b) the polypropylene segments and the poly(ethylene-co-propylene) segments have been synthesized in the presence of an olefin polymerization catalyst comprising an organometallic compound and a solid catalyst component comprising either titanium and a halogen or titanium, magnesium, and a halogen. The block copolymer has a weight-average molecular weight of 100,000 or higher, is suitable for producing general-purpose molded articles, and has an excellent balance among mechanical properties, impact resistance, thermal properties, transparency, moldability, etc.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un copolymère séquencé propylène/éthylène contenant de 5 à 100 % (non compris) en poids de motifs poly(éthylène-copropylène), et un total de 2 % à 95 % en poids d'éthylène. Ce copolymère présente les caractéristiques suivantes : (a) il comprend des motifs polypropylène liées par des liaisons chimiques à des motifs poly(éthylène-copropylène), et (b) les motifs poylpropylène et les motifs poly(éthylène-copropylène) ont été synthétisés en présence d'un catalyseur de polymérisation oléfinique comprenant un composé organométallique et un composant catalyseur solide contenant soit du titane et un halogène, soit du titane, du magnésium et un halogène. Ce copolymère séquencé a un poids moléculaire égal ou supérieur à 100 000, et convient pour la production d'articles moulés d'usage général. Il présente en outre un excellent équilibre entre les propriétés, mécaniques, la résistance aux chocs, les propriétés thermiques, la transparence, l'aptitude au moulage etc.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/lega